<description>&lt;p&gt;President De la Espriella has ordered temporary militarization of Cúcuta and deployed troops to the Venezuelan border city amid rising violence, while also expanding the military presence in other border areas. The government charged nine former FARC commanders with war crimes and is conducting an anti-narcotics operation that has raised questions over civilian killings. US troops have been deployed to Colombia as Washington forges a new Operation Condor across the Americas, and Salvadoran forces are being sent to Haiti with Colombian support. 225 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxPc1ZSZlJhZnhXbWtIVDhwaTZWeGVLQlo5LVhGZ3kzcnVicUQ5dXVEOFNCWDlZcHR6M2YyV2NVN0pCTGphYy1sTlpLbXp0dXB5ekk0c0p2Z1A5N3AxVTB6dGVxajVKLTJHcGFiVW82a21HenJTdkQzcndRV21uaXc5R1ZTWk9JVlUwU3B2OVlyYVNSakZ3d0JVcWRPY3pzcG94UlJXZGd3?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijgFBVV95cUxOWXduQndkRk90N2RLZlFzdldxZ2pFclJSa05lbkIzX05lSFNubEpSaG5pUzkwNWhFcjNISXkzTXNPaFpaVURwS3lGQUxranpLUmpKM1liRXRtanZlbU54VzBXMzVCY1lLNWE1MXpReGdseWNNRXdlNGZ1RVBoNzVwenlLcEg4b0RBWTB4TFBB?oc=5&quot;&gt;Yahoo Sports&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiaEFVX3lxTE0zNE50Zk0zSVdkRFNrb1lCcmd5eVp0R2hZd3FnaVc4WTc5SFhtbUN1SUxhWXpkR1hwNGVTYjFrLVRocll5TDhicERHX3R3elNiTXBQcjU1dFhLTFpPMFl0TUtIaXRMQzJG?oc=5&quot;&gt;World Socialist Web Site&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiywFBVV95cUxQbzBHSVZtU1pzbk9zQ0dNQUNzNVhsanJJY0RsUERUanI0T1JURkZSWUtWdHRqSW8wanBTRVJtamlUM0lRN0hTZUI1NVB2WW9ocjNKVnF3UXFrZjBsVUJPaFFqWi1NZjRuZ3Z4R1JxNHc0NWJxenBoQ0t2ZGk3bFBwMXJjcFh1QjVId2dJY3lMZlliLXFHUzlEY3Mwdk9XT1JZS3RnUF